{"year":"2024","content":[{"type":"text","content_text":"The 96th Academy Awards ceremony took place on March 10, 2024, at the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, hosted by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 78303, 'screen_type': person}\">Jimmy Kimmel</a> for the fourth time. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 872585, 'screen_type': movie}\">Oppenheimer</a> (2023), by <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 525, 'screen_type': person}\">Christopher Nolan</a>, was the big winner, with seven awards, including Best Picture, Director, Actor (<a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 2037, 'screen_type': person}\">Cillian Murphy</a>) and Supporting Actor (<a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 3223, 'screen_type': person}\">Robert Downey Jr.</a>). <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 792307, 'screen_type': movie}\">Poor Things</a> (2023) won four statuettes, including Best Actress for <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 54693, 'screen_type': person}\">Emma Stone</a>, and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 467244, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Zone of Interest</a> (2023) took home two."},{"type":"block_special","title":"Records","description":"<a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 467244, 'screen_type': movie}\">The Zone of Interest</a> (2023), winner of Best Sound, and <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 940721, 'screen_type': movie}\">Godzilla Minus One</a> (2023), winner of Best Visual Effects, were the first non-English-language films to win in those categories. <a href=\"https://_{type: 'screen', 'id': 1183917, 'screen_type': person}\">Lily Gladstone</a> became the first Native American nominated for Best Actress, and Billie Eilish, who won Best Original Song for \"What Was I Made For?\", became the youngest person to win two Oscars."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Picture","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":872585,"name":"Oppenheimer","image_path":"/dUPQszWoRSE9FucJTbVp2bwEi9G.jpg","director":"Christopher Nolan","winn